WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.601
Welcome, welcome, welcome to "The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:03.601 --> 00:00:06.534
Thank you for being here. Thank you for watching.

00:00:06.534 --> 00:00:08.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.701 --> 00:00:10.834
Well, guys, everyone is talking about this.

00:00:10.834 --> 00:00:14.501
Netflix just announced that for the first time in over a decade,

00:00:14.501 --> 00:00:18.200
they lost subscribers, and now their stock is crashing.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:19.400
-Ooh. -Yeah.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:20.734
Not only did their stock plummet,

00:00:20.734 --> 00:00:22.734
but it turns out that all the cash they had in the bank

00:00:22.734 --> 00:00:24.501
was just cake.

00:00:24.501 --> 00:00:27.968
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.968 --> 00:00:30.467
Yeah, apparently raising their subscription fee

00:00:30.467 --> 00:00:33.667
every eight seconds wasn't such a good idea.

00:00:33.667 --> 00:00:35.667
Right now Netflix is so desperate for money,

00:00:35.667 --> 00:00:37.667
they're now googling "Is there a real life 'Squid Game'?"

00:00:37.667 --> 00:00:40.167
It's sad.

00:00:40.167 --> 00:00:41.767
Netflix is blaming their losses

00:00:41.767 --> 00:00:45.667
on fierce competition, inflation, and Russia.

00:00:45.667 --> 00:00:47.767
When he heard that, President Biden was like,

00:00:47.767 --> 00:00:51.300
"hey, get your own excuses. That's..."

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:53.467
But now Netflix says they're open to launching

00:00:53.467 --> 00:00:55.868
lower-priced streaming plans with ads.

00:00:55.868 --> 00:00:59.033
[ Audience groans ]

00:00:59.033 --> 00:01:00.968
That's right. Entertainment with commercials.

00:01:00.968 --> 00:01:03.701
It's an innovative new concept called "television."

00:01:03.701 --> 00:01:05.534
Very interesting.

00:01:05.534 --> 00:01:07.133
Yep, Netflix is losing money.

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:09.234
You can tell it's having an effect on all of their shows.

00:01:09.234 --> 00:01:12.100
For instance, "Emily in Paris" is now

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:13.334
"Emily in Pittsburgh."

00:01:13.334 --> 00:01:14.901
-Oh. -It's still good, but, yeah.

00:01:14.901 --> 00:01:16.133
-Wow.

00:01:16.133 --> 00:01:18.968
-Also, "The Crown"

00:01:18.968 --> 00:01:22.300
is now "The Hat."

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:24.400
And finally, "Bridgerton" is now

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:26.334
"American Girl Dolls Being Rubbed Against Each Other

00:01:26.334 --> 00:01:28.000
With Human Hands."

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:30.133
[ Applause ]

00:01:30.133 --> 00:01:33.601
I'll still watch it, but...

00:01:33.601 --> 00:01:35.100
Well, this is nice.

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:36.601
I read that next month President Biden

00:01:36.601 --> 00:01:39.400
is returning to his alma mater, the University of Delaware,

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.601
to deliver the commencement speech.

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:43.200
Yep, freshmen are actually invited

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:45.534
to this graduation because when Biden's done speaking

00:01:45.534 --> 00:01:46.968
they'll be seniors.

00:01:46.968 --> 00:01:48.501
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.501 --> 00:01:51.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:55.934 --> 00:01:58.067
But I'm sure Biden's address will inspire kids,

00:01:58.067 --> 00:02:00.300
especially when he says, "I'm living proof that if you

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:03.334
follow your dreams you can achieve them...in 60 years."

00:02:03.334 --> 00:02:05.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:08.300
Well, I saw that the CDC has officially launched a new center

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:12.067
that will forecast outbreaks of infectious diseases.

00:02:12.067 --> 00:02:14.100
It raises a lot of questions like, uh,

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.467
"Isn't that what they did?"

00:02:15.467 --> 00:02:17.334
I mean...

00:02:17.334 --> 00:02:20.400
That's what the CDC does, right?

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:23.033
It feels sort of like CNN launching CNN Plus.

00:02:23.033 --> 00:02:26.400
It's like, wait. What are we -- What are we doing here? Yeah.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:27.734
Listen to this.

00:02:27.734 --> 00:02:30.000
Today Vin Diesel announced that the title of the next

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.667
"Fast and Furious" movie is "Fast X."

00:02:32.667 --> 00:02:34.868
[ Audience oohs ]

00:02:34.868 --> 00:02:37.067
It actually sounds like an over-the-counter laxative.

00:02:37.067 --> 00:02:39.033
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.033 --> 00:02:40.567
-Zoink!

00:02:40.567 --> 00:02:42.334
[ Drum beat ]

00:02:42.334 --> 00:02:44.267
-It actually sounds like a FedEx knockoff

00:02:44.267 --> 00:02:46.434
where a guy named Dennis shows up with your package.

00:02:46.434 --> 00:02:48.400
"Hey, you ordered Fast X?"

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:50.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.167 --> 00:02:51.400
Hey, get this, everyone.

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:53.400
NASA just released a new report where they say

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:56.267
their biggest priority is probing Uranus.

00:02:56.267 --> 00:02:58.701
-Ohh.

00:02:58.701 --> 00:03:01.033
Come on. -Higgins, do you want --

00:03:01.033 --> 00:03:03.534
Do you know anything about Uranus?

00:03:03.534 --> 00:03:06.200
-Well, I know it's the seventh planet from the sun.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:07.667
-Interesting.

00:03:07.667 --> 00:03:10.701
-It's also the third-largest planet in the solar system.

00:03:10.701 --> 00:03:12.701
It's almost four times larger than Earth.

00:03:12.701 --> 00:03:15.133
-That's it? -Um...

00:03:15.133 --> 00:03:18.968
It also reminds me of, you know, "your anus,"

00:03:18.968 --> 00:03:20.367
you know, like, the words. -Yeah, that's what I --

00:03:20.367 --> 00:03:21.934
-Is it the Red Planet?

00:03:21.934 --> 00:03:24.400
No, it's a brown planet, right? Uranus?

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:25.968
-I -- I wouldn't know.

00:03:25.968 --> 00:03:27.667
Are you talking about Uranus as a whole?

00:03:27.667 --> 00:03:30.033
-Yeah. Not a black hole, though.

00:03:30.033 --> 00:03:31.367
That's a different... -Yeah, different thing.

00:03:31.367 --> 00:03:33.834
-...celestial body. -Thank you.

00:03:33.834 --> 00:03:36.467
Well, guys, today is 4/20,

00:03:36.467 --> 00:03:38.667
and oddly enough, tomorrow... [ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:38.667 --> 00:03:40.801
Yeah. Happy 4/20, everyone. Tomorrow --

00:03:40.801 --> 00:03:42.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:49.267
Oddly enough, tomorrow, the sale of recreational weed

00:03:49.267 --> 00:03:51.300
will begin in New Jersey.

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:52.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:52.934 --> 00:03:54.868
Yeah. That's right.

00:03:54.868 --> 00:03:58.033
One day after 4/20.

00:03:58.033 --> 00:03:59.467
I mean, really?

00:03:59.467 --> 00:04:02.100
That's like Chipotle offering free guac on Seis de Mayo.

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:04.100
You know what I'm saying?

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:06.100
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.367 --> 00:04:11.334
Meanwhile, police say that a man in West Virginia was arrested

00:04:11.334 --> 00:04:13.033
after he was pulled over,

00:04:13.033 --> 00:04:14.801
and instead of handing officers his registration,

00:04:14.801 --> 00:04:16.467
he gave them his meth.

00:04:16.467 --> 00:04:19.767
[ Laughter ]

00:04:19.767 --> 00:04:22.734
His lawyer was like, "Your Honor -- I got nothing.

00:04:22.734 --> 00:04:25.334
I..."

00:04:25.334 --> 00:04:27.167
And, finally, did you guys see the picture

00:04:27.167 --> 00:04:29.033
of French President Emmanuel Macron

00:04:29.033 --> 00:04:30.400
that was going around yesterday?

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:32.734
It went viral because his shirt is unbuttoned

00:04:32.734 --> 00:04:34.467
and he's showing a lot of chest hair.

00:04:34.467 --> 00:04:36.167
Here it is. Here it is right -- Yeah.

00:04:36.167 --> 00:04:38.167
-Whoa. -[ Audience oohs ]

00:04:38.167 --> 00:04:40.934
-Yeah, well, Macron is running for re-election right now,

00:04:40.934 --> 00:04:43.200
and he actually asked us if he could premiere

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:45.834
a new campaign song on our show tonight.

00:04:45.834 --> 00:04:47.767
So, ladies and gentlemen,

00:04:47.767 --> 00:04:51.267
please welcome French President Emmanuel Macron.

00:04:51.267 --> 00:04:53.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:53.968 --> 00:05:04.033
♪♪

00:05:04.033 --> 00:05:06.734
[French accent] ♪ Bonjour, it is me ♪

00:05:06.734 --> 00:05:09.267
♪ With my chest hair, you see ♪

00:05:09.267 --> 00:05:11.901
♪ Do you think I'm sexy? ♪

00:05:11.901 --> 00:05:15.467
♪ I sure hope you say oui ♪

00:05:15.467 --> 00:05:20.167
♪ I have good policies for ze economy ♪

00:05:20.167 --> 00:05:26.400
♪ I shall make my VP Emily in Paris ♪

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:28.667
♪ I'm as French as can be ♪

00:05:28.667 --> 00:05:31.200
♪ I can get you in free ♪

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:33.834
♪ To ze patisserie ♪

00:05:33.834 --> 00:05:36.567
♪ The chef is Ratatouille ♪

00:05:40.734 --> 00:05:44.033
♪ We can nibble ze brie ♪

00:05:44.033 --> 00:05:46.601
♪ Smoke a cig by the sea ♪

00:05:46.601 --> 00:05:49.033
♪ Give my chest hair a squeeze ♪

00:05:49.033 --> 00:05:52.534
